# React Native performance
- Diagnose measured render or interaction bottlenecks before adding memoization. React Compiler may already handle many cases.
- For potentially long datasets prefer FlatList or SectionList (or the app's existing virtualized-list solution), with stable item keys; avoid rendering large arrays in ScrollView.
- Never use array indices as keys for reorderable/mutable lists.
- Avoid expensive synchronous computation inside render; avoid unnecessary state, derived-state effects and cascaded updates.
- Avoid inline anonymous renderItem only when it actually causes measurable or documented problems; do not over-apply useMemo/useCallback.
- Choose properly sized images, clean up listeners/timers and cancel obsolete async work where supported.
- Keep accessibility, touch targets, safe areas, keyboard behavior and Android/iOS platform differences in scope.
- Confirm optimizations with a before/after observable outcome when possible.
